**Given:**

Rate of Interest (R) = 12% per annum

Interest (SI) = ₹6,000 per annum

**Formula used:**

SI = dfrac{P times R times T}{100} 

Where, P = Principal amount

**Calculation:**

6000 = dfrac{P times 12 times 1}{100} 

⇒ 6000 = dfrac{12P}{100} 

⇒ P = dfrac{6000 times 100}{12} 

⇒ P = 50,000

**∴ The correct answer is option 2.**
